# Line endings.
#
# SkillGuard's whole reproducibility promise rests on the content digest, and
# `sgdir-v1` hashes bytes. If a Windows checkout converts LF to CRLF, the same
# commit produces a different digest — and a lockfile written on Linux would not
# verify on Windows. Forcing LF on text files makes the checked-out bytes
# identical on every platform.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binaries; only text files are normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never touched by the normaliser.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
